==History==
2016
*The Baby Dragon [[Cards|card]] was added with Clash Royale's game launch on 4/1/2016.
*On 29/2/2016, the [[Version History#March 2016 Update (29/2/2016)|March 2016 Update]], changed the Baby Dragon so that it would no longer stop its attack if its target dies during the attack animation. It also decreased the Baby Dragon's sight range to 5.5 tiles (from 6 tiles).
*On 3/5/2016, the [[Version History#May 2016 Update (3/5/2016)|May 2016 Update]], fixed the "range bug" and decreased the Baby Dragon's range to 3 tiles (from 3.5 tiles), but its effective range remained unchanged.
*On 24/8/2016, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (24/8/2016)|Balance Update]], decreased the Baby Dragon's attack time interval to 1.6 seconds (from 1.8 seconds) and its first attack time interval to 0.3 seconds (from 0.5 seconds).
2017
*On 13/2/2017, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (13/2/2017)|Balance Update]], increased the Baby Dragon's range to 3.5 tiles (from 3 tiles).
2018
*On 6/8/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (6/8/2018)|Balance Update]], decreased the Baby Dragon's attack time interval to 1.5 seconds (from 1.6 seconds), but allow it to be knocked back.
*On 5/9/2018, the [[Version History#September%202018%20Update%20(5/9/2018)|September 2018 Update]], changed it so that {{Rarity|Epic}} cards start at Level 6 and end at Level 13 (from 1 to 8). It also changed the Baby Dragon's card description. It used to read "''Flying troop that deals area damage. Baby dragons hatch cute, hungry and ready for a barbeque.''"
2019
*On 4/11/2019, a [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (4/11/2019)|Balance Update]], decreased the Baby Dragon's hitpoints by 4%.
*On 26/11/2019, the [[Version History#End%20of%20November%202019%20Update%20(26/11/2019)|End of November 2019 Update]], added a card render to the Baby Dragon's card info screen.
2020
*On 5/5/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (5/5/2020)|Balance Update]], decreased the Baby Dragon's hitpoints by 6.5%.
*On 30/7/2020, a maintenance break, changed the Baby Dragon's card render.
2021
*On 7/6/2021, the [[Version History#Summer%202021%20Update%20(7/6/2021)|Summer 2021 Update]], moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Baby Dragon from [[Training Camp]] to Bone Pit.
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13).
2022
*On 26/10/2022, the [[Version History#2022%20Quarter%203%20Update%20(26/10/2022)|2022 Quarter 3 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Baby Dragon from Bone Pit to P.E.K.K.A's Playhouse. It also added the No Escape [[Card Mastery]] task for the Baby Dragon.
2023
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14).
2025
*On 8/1/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (8/1/2025)|Balance Update]] increased the Baby Dragon's area radius to 1.5 tiles (from 1.2 tiles).
*On 31/3/2025, the [[Version History#2025 Quarter 1 Update (31/3/2025)|2025 Quarter 1 Update]], increased the Baby Dragon's damage by 0.62%.
*On 1/9/2025, the [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (1/9/2025)|September 2025 Update]], added the Baby Dragon's Evolution.
*On 24/11/2025, the [[Version History#Level 16 Update (24/11/2025)|Level 16 Update]] increased the Level Cap of all cards to 16 (from 15).
2026

* On 6/7/2026, a Balance Update, increased the Baby Dragon's damage by 4%

