==Trivia==
*The Baby Dragon resemble [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_dragon dragons from European cultures], being reptilian legendary creatures, often depicted as winged, horned, and capable of breathing fire.
**The [[Inferno Dragon]] is of the same breed as the Baby Dragon, but the Inferno Dragon moves slower, and has slightly more hitpoints, possibly because it carries extra equipment and wears a helmet. However, they are otherwise identical in terms of animations and deployment sound effects.
**A Trainer in the [[Training Camp]] is called Trainer Dragon and uses 2 dragon [[cards]] in their [[Battle Decks|deck]], one of them being Baby Dragon, and the other being Inferno Dragon.
*It is 1 of 3 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] that are “miniature” versions of another troop in Clash of Clans, the others being the [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]] and [[Electro Dragon]]. They are smaller versions of [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Dragon Dragon], [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/P.E.K.K.A P.E.K.K.A], and [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Electro_Dragon Electro Dragon], respectively.
**In the Arabic, Thai, and Finnish language settings of the game, the Baby Dragon's name translates to "Little Dragon".
*The Baby Dragon is 1 of 17 troops that inspired a troop in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Spear Goblins]], [[Bomber]], [[Bats]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Minion Horde]], [[Firecracker]], [[Battle Ram]], [[Ice Golem]], [[Zappies]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Ram Rider]], Inferno Dragon, [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], and [[Night Witch]].
**Unlike its Clash of Clans counterpart, the Baby Dragon in Clash Royale does not get enraged when alone.
**Before the game's release, the Dragon from Clash of Clans was originally planned to be in Clash Royale, however, due to Dragon's wings being too large that covers a great part of the battlefield, it was replaced by the Baby Dragon.
*The Baby Dragon is one of the first troop cards to be featured in a Trainer's deck, alongside the [[Minions]], [[Archers]], [[Knight]], Spear Goblins, [[Goblins]], Bomber, [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], Minion Horde, [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Musketeer]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Prince]], and [[Balloon]].
*The Baby Dragon is one of the first troop cards to receive a card render, alongside the Archers, Knight, Goblins, Bomber, Skeletons, Barbarians, Bats, [[Royal Recruits]], Skeleton Barrel, [[Rascals]], Musketeer, Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, [[Flying Machine]], Hog Rider, [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], Zappies, [[Elixir Golem]], Skeleton Army, Witch, P.E.K.K.A, Prince, Balloon, Giant Skeleton, [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], Electro Dragon, [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Mega Knight]], Ram Rider, Miner, Royal Ghost, Ice Wizard, [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], [[Lava Hound]], Night Witch, and [[Fisherman]].
*The Baby Dragon is 1 of 4 troops that has been featured in the [[Treasure Hunt#Dragon Hunt|Dragon Hunt]] sub-[[:Category:Modes|mode]] of the [[Treasure Hunt]] game mode, the others being [[Skeleton Dragons]], Electro Dragon, and Inferno Dragon.
*Baby Dragon's wings are undersized. It doesn't seem to have enough wingspan to support flight, yet this has no impact on gameplay.
*The Baby Dragon, along with the Minions, Bomber, Skeletons, Skeleton Dragons, [[Ice Spirit]], Mini P.E.K.K.A, [[Mega Minion]], Ice Golem, Dart Goblin, Elixir Golem, [[Goblin Cage|Goblin Brawler]], [[Guards]], P.E.K.K.A, Giant Skeleton, [[Golem]], Wall Breakers, Bowler, [[Executioner]], Mega Knight, Inferno Dragon, Royal Ghost, and Lava Hound, are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Monsters monster] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*The Baby Dragon's gender has been confirmed as male, as the [https://youtu.be/tbiICYsRdGc Baby Dragon's commercial] referred to Baby Dragon as "he".
*According to the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4M_PPPCN19E Electro Dragon's intro video], it is implied that the Baby Dragon, Electro Dragon, and Inferno Dragon are brothers.
*The Baby Dragon is the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Baby Dragon is the subject of 4 [[Emotes]].
***In the card's image, the Baby Dragon's tongue is blue, but in its Emotes, the Baby Dragon's tongue is red. This does not depict an opponent Baby Dragon, as the spikes on its back are still blue in its Emotes.
**The Baby Dragon is the subject of a few [[Battle Banners|Battle Banner]] items.
***The King and Dragon decoration is created by Myoho.
***The Pumpkin Barrage decoration is a reference to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_Goblin Green Goblin]. Its description says "''What a nice Dragon, sharing these pumpkins with us. Wait a second, are these explosive pumpkins?!''", which is also a reference to the same character.
***The Dragon Trio decoration's description says "''There's a Queen somewhere who is a big fan of three dragons.''", which is a reference to [https://gameofthrones.fandom.com/wiki/Daenerys_Targaryen Daenerys Targaryen].
*The Baby Dragon was featured in the winning decks of multiple Clash Royale Tournaments. More specifically:
**The Baby Dragon was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/1fuCnNBTqBU?feature=share King's Cup Tournament], by a player called TMD YAOYAO.
**The Baby Dragon was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/cmBlEI-aDoo?si=UoD1Sit2YvQR19xs Clash Royale League 2019 Tournament], by a player called Surgical Goblin.
**The Baby Dragon was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/pRfrjMiHbQA?si=P2kVLJUlXH1SZoHm Clash Royale League 2021 Tournament], by a player called Mugi.
*On 6/6/2023, the Baby Dragon was supposed to receive a sight range decrease to 5 tiles (from 5.5 tiles), but this change [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-48-balance-wip was pulled back last minute].

